WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:19.293
Daisy, and Grace were kicking a ball on the school playground.

2
00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.956
When the bell rang, Kaleem groaned.

3
00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:31.620
is over already?"

4
00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:33.272
Daisy smiled.

5
00:00:33.292 --> 00:00:35.073
"It's almost the end of the day.

6
00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:38.715
That means it's almost one day closer to our summer vacation."

7
00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:40.936
Kaleem's face brightened.

8
00:00:46.258 --> 00:00:48.039
one day closer to our beach trip!"

9
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.640
He waved away a cloud of gnats.

10
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.622
"Ugh, where did these pesky bugs come from?"

11
00:00:56.642 --> 00:01:00.884
"There are lots of gnats around now that spring is here," Grace said.

12
00:01:02.624 --> 00:01:03.845
"Mosquitoes too.

13
00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:05.946
When are you going to the beach?"

14
00:01:05.966 --> 00:01:09.588
"Our families always go in July," Daisy said.

15
00:01:14.812 --> 00:01:17.013
never been to the beach," Grace said.

16
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.034
"Is it fun?"

17
00:01:18.054 --> 00:01:22.516
"Yes!" Kaleem told her about it as they walked inside the building.

18
00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.120
Daisy waved away more gnats.

19
00:01:29.544 --> 00:01:32.786
She loved all animals, but gnats were annoying.

20
00:01:36.608 --> 00:01:37.549
Inside, Mr.

21
00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:40.030
Neal clapped to get everyone's attention.

22
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.852
"It's time for science, class.

23
00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:46.254
We're going to do one last project before the end of the year."

24
00:01:46.274 --> 00:01:48.095
"What is it?"

25
00:01:48.455 --> 00:01:49.195
Kaleem asked.

26
00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:50.756
The teacher smiled.

27
00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.557
"I think you'll like this one.

28
00:01:53.198 --> 00:01:54.839
It's about backyard wildlife."

29
00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.402
Daisy sat up straighter in her chair.

30
00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.645
Wildlife? That sounded interesting!

31
00:02:02.665 --> 00:02:08.570
"I want you to think about how people and wild animals exist side by side," Mr.

32
00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.171
Neal said.

33
00:02:09.191 --> 00:02:12.173
"You'll take photos of a wild backyard animal.

34
00:02:12.814 --> 00:02:14.435
Then you'll research that animal.

35
00:02:14.936 --> 00:02:17.258
Learn about where and how your animal lives.

36
00:02:18.279 --> 00:02:21.181
Think about how their lives intersect with people's lives.

37
00:02:21.782 --> 00:02:24.144
Next week you'll tell the class what you've discovered."

38
00:02:25.776 --> 00:02:29.279
"I see deer in my yard all the time," Raj said.

39
00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:31.761
"I'm studying raccoons."

40
00:02:32.261 --> 00:02:33.122
Parker grinned.

41
00:02:33.142 --> 00:02:36.264
"Their masks make them look like little bandits!"

42
00:02:37.805 --> 00:02:45.410
Other kids named their favorite animals: rabbits, squirrels, birds, grasshoppers, frogs, foxes, and others.

43
00:02:48.273 --> 00:02:49.914
Kaleem leaned toward Daisy.

44
00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.756
"This will be easy for you," he whispered.

45
00:02:53.428 --> 00:02:55.509
"You can just ask the animals about themselves."

46
00:02:57.229 --> 00:02:59.130
Daisy grinned and then shushed him.

47
00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.551
She couldn't wait to start this project!

48
00:03:04.131 --> 00:03:06.572
Beatrice was sipping nectar from a flower.

49
00:03:07.532 --> 00:03:10.013
Students started pouring out of the school building.

50
00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.694
Beatrice buzzed over to Daisy and her friends.

51
00:03:13.714 --> 00:03:18.835
"Daisy, what animal are you going to study?"

52
00:03:19.195 --> 00:03:20.015
Grace asked.

53
00:03:20.035 --> 00:03:21.836
"I'm studying chipmunks.

54
00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.669
They're so cute!"

55
00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:27.312
"Um Daisy glanced at Beatrice.

56
00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:29.753
"Maybe I'll focus on bumblebees."

57
00:03:29.773 --> 00:03:31.895
"What? No!"

58
00:03:32.395 --> 00:03:36.078
Alarmed, Beatrice darted into Daisy's hair to hide.

59
00:03:36.098 --> 00:03:39.140
"People might notice me following you around.

60
00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.021
Choose another animal!"

61
00:03:45.464 --> 00:03:48.526
going to study an animal that's active at night," Kaleem said.

62
00:03:48.546 --> 00:03:52.445
"Bats!" "Right, bats are nocturnal."

63
00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.627
Daisy was still thinking about what to choose.

64
00:03:55.647 --> 00:03:58.608
"Hmm, maybe I won't do bumblebees.

65
00:03:59.149 --> 00:04:00.109
But I'm not sure yet.

66
00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:01.830
I have to think about it some more."

67
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.692
"Phew!" Beatrice thought.

68
00:04:05.673 --> 00:04:08.954
She was relieved that she'd talked Daisy out of choosing bees.

69
00:04:10.275 --> 00:04:11.896
Then something else dawned on her.

70
00:04:12.256 --> 00:04:15.819
Daisy had just said she wasn't sure which animal to study.

71
00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:23.199
"Choosing one should be simple for an animal ambassador like Daisy," Beatrice thought.

72
00:04:23.219 --> 00:04:25.441
"I'd better help her with this.

73
00:04:26.182 --> 00:04:30.067
Otherwise the Council of Animals might think they didn't choose the right human!"
